From bfa45fb4e384b0abf3d9f402d3e5928383c79870 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gauthier Piarrette <gauthierpiarrette@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:16:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Keep attachment-less render passes within Apple GPUs' size
 limit

A render pass without attachments takes its size from the render area and its layer count from the
rendering info. vkd3d-proton renders D3D12 UAV-only draws in such a pass at the device maximums,
16384x16384 and 2048 layers, and on Apple GPUs every command buffer holding one ends with "Internal
Error (0000010d:Internal Error)" (IOGPUCommandQueueErrorDomain 269) without running. In Microsoft
Flight Simulator 2024 that is about 70 command buffers by the end of the world load, each one taking
the texture streaming work it carried with it: block noise in the PFD terrain, the MFD map and the
compass minimap, and garbage ground textures.

A Metal-only test (a pass without attachments, one pipeline without color attachment writing an
R8Uint 2D array from the fragment shader) fails the same way. On an M1 Pro, 16384x16384 fails from
256 to 512 layers and 8192x8192 at 2048 layers. On an M4, 16384x16384 fails at 2048 layers. The same
passes work with one layer, and 4096x4096 works with 2048 layers.

The pass now keeps width x height x layers within 2^34 by lowering the layer count. Layers only
matter to shaders that write a render target array index, and none of the game's do. With the
change, a full test flight (world load, two minutes parked, takeoff roll) had no failed command
buffer, against about 70 by Ready to fly in each run before, and the noise in the cockpit displays
and the ground textures was gone.
---
 MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCommandBuffer.mm | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCommandBuffer.mm b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCommandBuffer.mm
index 8c24deb..94212e2 100644
--- a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCommandBuffer.mm
+++ b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCommandBuffer.mm
@@ -827,6 +827,23 @@ static MVKBarrierStage commandUseToBarrierStage(MVKCommandUse use) {
         }
     }
 
+	// A render pass without attachments, sized at the device maximums (vkd3d-proton renders D3D12 UAV-only draws in a
+	// 16384x16384 pass of 2048 layers), fails on Apple GPUs: the command buffer ends with "Internal Error
+	// (0000010d:Internal Error)" without running. A Metal-only test fails from 256-512 layers at 16384x16384 on an
+	// M1 Pro and at 2048 layers on an M4, and works with one layer, so width x height x layers is kept within 2^34 by
+	// lowering the layer count. Only shaders that write a render target array index of that many layers need them.
+	if ( !mtlRPDesc.depthAttachment.texture && !mtlRPDesc.stencilAttachment.texture && mtlRPDesc.renderTargetArrayLength > 1 ) {
+		bool hasColor = false;
+		for (uint32_t caIdx = 0; caIdx < kMVKMaxColorAttachmentCount && !hasColor; caIdx++) {
+			hasColor = mtlRPDesc.colorAttachments[caIdx].texture != nil;
+		}
+		const uint64_t maxPixelLayers = 1ull << 34;
+		uint64_t pixels = (uint64_t)mtlRPDesc.renderTargetWidth * (uint64_t)mtlRPDesc.renderTargetHeight;
+		if ( !hasColor && pixels && pixels * mtlRPDesc.renderTargetArrayLength > maxPixelLayers ) {
+			mtlRPDesc.renderTargetArrayLength = (NSUInteger)std::max<uint64_t>(1, maxPixelLayers / pixels);
+		}
+	}
+
 	// If programmable sample positions are supported, set them into the render pass descriptor.
 	// If no custom sample positions are established, size will be zero,
 	// and Metal will default to using default sample postions.
-- 
